Third-party services and their terms

Invidious                     AGPL-3.0
  https://github.com/iv-org/invidious
  Sieve consumes its public JSON API. It does not bundle or modify Invidious.

SponsorBlock                  database: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  https://sponsor.ajay.app
  Segment data is queried by hash prefix and cached locally.

DeArrow                       database: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  https://dearrow.ajay.app
  Crowd-voted titles and thumbnail timestamps, likewise by hash prefix.

Sieve uses SponsorBlock and DeArrow data under those terms: it is a
non-commercial personal tool, it attributes both projects in its interface and
its documentation, and it does not redistribute their databases. A local cache
of query results is kept for the operator's own use only.

Anyone deploying Sieve commercially must review those terms independently; the
non-commercial clause applies to the data, not to Sieve's own code.

